        DayContent(
            scriptureReference: "Philippians 3:13-14",
            scriptureText: "Brothers and sisters, I do not consider myself yet to have taken hold of it. But one thing I do: Forgetting what is behind and straining toward what is ahead, I press on toward the goal to win the prize for which God has called me heavenward in Christ Jesus.",
            devotionalTitle: "Pressing Forward",
            devotionalText: "Paul — who had persecuted Christians, watched Stephen die, and made devastating mistakes — chose to forget what was behind. Not because the past didn't matter, but because the future mattered more. Pressing on requires letting go. You can't run forward while looking backward. Today, make Paul's declaration your own: I press on.",
            prayerText: "Lord, I forget what is behind and press on toward what is ahead. I refuse to let my past define my future. The prize You've called me toward is greater than any failure behind me. Give me the strength to keep pressing forward, even when the past tries to pull me back. I press on in Christ Jesus. In Jesus' name, amen.",
