            devotionalText: "David knew what it was like to be stuck — in a slimy pit with no footing. But God didn't just pull him out; He set him on a rock. Not shifting sand. A rock. And then He gave him a new song. Your starting over isn't just about escaping the pit — it's about finding solid ground and discovering a new reason to sing. God does all three.",
            prayerText: "Lord, lift me out of the pit I've been stuck in. Set my feet on solid rock and give me a firm place to stand. Put a new song in my mouth — not a song of shame, but a hymn of praise. I've waited for You, and I trust You to rescue me. Give me solid ground today. In Jesus' name, amen.",
            reflectionPrompt: "What 'pit' has God already begun lifting you out of?",
            actionSteps: ["Identify the 'pit' and the 'rock' — what you're leaving and what you're standing on", "Sing, hum, or play a worship song as your 'new song' today"]
