            devotionalText: "Starting over is impossible when you're drowning in condemnation. But Paul declares the truth: there is now NO condemnation. Not 'less condemnation' or 'condemnation for the small stuff.' None. Zero. If you're in Christ, the verdict is in and you're free. Shame is not from God. Conviction leads to change; condemnation leads to paralysis. Walk in freedom today.",
            prayerText: "Lord, I receive this truth: there is no condemnation for me in Christ Jesus. I reject the shame that tries to keep me stuck. I am free — fully forgiven, completely accepted. Help me walk in this freedom today. When condemnation knocks, remind me of this verse. I am not condemned. I am Yours. In Jesus' name, amen.",
            reflectionPrompt: "Is condemnation keeping you from starting over? What would change if you truly believed there is none?",
            actionSteps: ["Every time shame or condemnation surfaces today, say out loud 'No condemnation in Christ'", "Write a letter to yourself from God's perspective, expressing His forgiveness and freedom"]
