        DayContent(
            scriptureReference: "Micah 7:8",
            scriptureText: "Do not gloat over me, my enemy! Though I have fallen, I will rise. Though I sit in darkness, the Lord will be my light.",
            devotionalTitle: "I Will Rise",
            devotionalText: "Falling isn't failure — staying down is. Micah fell, sat in darkness, and faced enemies who celebrated his defeat. But his declaration is defiant: 'I will rise.' Not 'I might' or 'I hope to.' I will. And the darkness won't last because God is his light. Your fall doesn't define you. Your rising does. Get back up. The Lord is your light.",
            prayerText: "Lord, though I have fallen, I will rise. Though I sit in darkness, You are my light. Silence the voice of the enemy who gloats over my failure. Give me the strength and determination to get back up. My fall is not the end of my story. My rising is. Light my way forward. In Jesus' name, amen.",
            reflectionPrompt: "Can you declare 'I will rise' today? What does rising look like for you?",
            actionSteps: ["Stand up physically and say 'Though I have fallen, I will rise' as a declaration of faith", "Take one action today that represents getting back up"]
