            scriptureText: "For I know the plans I have for you, declares the Lord, plans to prosper you and not to harm you, plans to give you hope and a future.",
            devotionalTitle: "Plans for Your Future",
            devotionalText: "God spoke these words to people in exile — displaced, defeated, and far from home. Yet He declared plans for their prosperity, hope, and future. If God had plans for people in exile, He has plans for you in your starting over. Your detour hasn't derailed His plans. Your failure hasn't erased His future for you. Hope is not naive; it's anchored in God's declared intentions.",
            prayerText: "Lord, I hold onto Your plans for me — plans to prosper me, not harm me. Plans for hope and a future. Even though I feel like I'm in exile, You haven't forgotten me. My detours haven't derailed Your purposes. Give me hope for the future You've planned. I trust Your intentions for my life. In Jesus' name, amen.",
            reflectionPrompt: "Do you believe God still has good plans for your future despite your past?",
            actionSteps: ["Write Jeremiah 29:11 and place it where you'll see it daily", "Dream about one thing you want God to do in your future and share it with someone"]
