        DayContent(
            scriptureReference: "Genesis 50:20",
            scriptureText: "You intended to harm me, but God intended it for good to accomplish what is now being done, the saving of many lives.",
            devotionalTitle: "God Intended It for Good",
            devotionalText: "Joseph said this to the brothers who sold him into slavery. Years of suffering — betrayal, prison, false accusations — and Joseph could see God's hand in all of it. What was meant to destroy him became the vehicle for saving a nation. Your worst chapters may become God's greatest work. He doesn't waste pain. He redeems it for purposes bigger than you can see.",
            prayerText: "Lord, what was intended to harm me, You intend for good. I may not see the full picture yet, but I trust that You are redeeming my pain for a greater purpose. Take the worst chapters of my story and write something beautiful. Nothing is wasted in Your economy. In Jesus' name, amen.",
            reflectionPrompt: "Can you begin to see how God might use your worst experience for someone else's good?",
            actionSteps: ["Write down the hardest thing you've been through and ask God to show you His purpose in it", "Share your story of redemption with someone who needs hope"]
