        DayContent(
            scriptureReference: "Psalm 126:5-6",
            scriptureText: "Those who sow with tears will reap with songs of joy. Those who go out weeping, carrying seed to sow, will return with songs of joy, carrying sheaves with them.",
            devotionalTitle: "From Tears to Joy",
            devotionalText: "Starting over often begins with tears — tears of regret, loss, or exhaustion. But the psalmist says those tears are seeds. Every tear you've sown is producing a harvest of joy. You're not crying for nothing. Keep sowing, even through tears. Keep showing up, even when it hurts. The harvest is coming, and you'll return carrying sheaves and singing.",
            prayerText: "Lord, I've sown with tears. I've gone out weeping. But I trust Your promise that I will reap with songs of joy. Turn my tears into seeds and my pain into a harvest. I keep sowing in faith, trusting that joy is on the other side. I will return with songs of joy. In Jesus' name, amen.",
            reflectionPrompt: "What seeds have you been sowing through tears that might be ready for harvest?",
            actionSteps: ["Plant one 'seed' today — an act of faith, obedience, or hope — even if it costs tears", "Write down three things you're believing God for in this new season"]
